			<div class="content" id="post-content-3743075">
									

<p>I don't think the number of D-Class run through is so much the problem as what's being done with them after, that being just keeping them locked up. Seems to me that after a certain point, the Foundation would decide to start &#8230; well, &quot;recycling&quot; a lot of the transformed subjects in other projects, letting Dr. Snekcliffe keep fifty or so for her own little zoo.</p>
<p>Which would make a great deal of sense, I think. Let's say you have an anomaly that primarily or only affects canines. What could be better than having a dog with a human mind who can actually communitate with you as a subject? This would almost certainly buy a lot of patience and D-Class access.</p>
<p>And Dr. Snekcliffe can still get into trouble because it's quite likely that she stepped up the rate of transformation to an intolerable degree over time. 577 transformed subjects over the course of a couple of years or so? Not <em>too</em> awful. But transforming five or more of 'em every day for a week? Someone's probably gonna take notice, and the blue whale incident can still be the ultimate capper that makes the higher ups' patience run out.</p>

							</div>

								
					
