<p>All right. Initially I was going to keep 577 and just have it ride on &quot;over a period of time.&quot; However, I think it would be much better to qualify, rather than quantify, Ssscarcliffe's obsession. To that end, I've lowered the number to 177. I've also modified the interview log to give a time frame during which these 177 were carried out. I've also addressed how Snakecliffe was able to somewhat hide away these numbers.</p>
<p>Other supplementary changes borne from this topic include changing Noodlecliffe's first name from Allison to Stephanie for reasons those of you good with nicknames will figure out, and the integration of Jim North's excellent point about recycling animals with human minds. Ideally, this makes the entire article more realistic and also more reliant on quality of experimentation, rather than quantity. Thank you all for the feedback and I hope this reads better!</p>

